  "body": "  There is a bicontinuous ring isomorphism    Lean (chartDatum)  Lean (coefficientwise equivalence)  Lean (continuity)  Lean (continuous inverse)  Lean (finite-variable chart ≃ k⟨X⟩)  Lean (isometric identification)  Lean (W ↦ ϖX)   The datum lies in . Let be its separated completed quotient. Evaluation at and gives a continuous map . Conversely, evaluation of at the image of gives a continuous map in the other direction. The two maps are inverse by polynomial density, and the norm estimates in the two universal properties show that the isomorphism is isometric.  Apply with . It describes the rational chart as the ring of sums Under , this is precisely the model . Its sup norm is , because the term indexed by is multiplied by . The map from sends to .   "
